      <activity id="903b88ba-f41b-5401-902a-676452c7afcf" activityNameId="dc6dec02-12c5-534d-8164-4511babea947" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Photovoltaic panel, CIS, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Photovoltaic panel, CIS, at plant
Production of photovoltaic thin film modules by thermal vaporization in vacuum. The modules produced at Würth Solar have a size of 1.2m by 0.6m. The weight is 12.6kg. The efficiency is 10.8%. The rated nominal power is about 78Wp per module.;
Synonyms: Solarmodul, PV-module, copper indium selenide, thin film, CIGS; 
UUID: 66202301-7079-30d9-b690-96ff555e7275
Electricity use, materials, transport of materials, treatment of production wastes. Disposal after end of life. Process emissions not known (except Cd).
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Production technology of thin film CIS cells with thermal vaporization in vacuum.
Time period: Data refer to 2007. Production in 2006 was ramped up.
Production volume: 14.8 MW planned for 2007
Sampling: Literature data based on producer information. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_66202301-7079-30d9-b690-96ff555e7275.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
